# Immutable appearance rules. Resolution is shared by native and browser views.
import lib/sections.dl
import geometry.dl
import lib/check.dl

class:
    patterns:
        UI appearance
    members:
        rules as a pointer to UI appearance rule
        count as an integer

class:
    patterns:
        UI appearance rule
    members:
        kind as an integer
        number as a floating-point number
        ink as UI paint
        text as a C string
        appearance as a pointer to UI appearance

UI appearance reference means: a pointer to UI appearance
no UI appearance means: a static reference to @intrinsic("construct", UI appearance, @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI appearance rule), 0)
UI appearance rule {integer:kind} valued {a value:number} means: @intrinsic("construct", UI appearance rule, kind, number as a floating-point number, UI ink 0 0 0, "", no UI appearance)
UI appearance rule {integer:kind} colored {UI paint:ink} means: @intrinsic("construct", UI appearance rule, kind, 0.0, ink, "", no UI appearance)

section appearance {name}:
    declares: name
    result: UI appearance reference
    body:
        rules: many UI appearance rule
    value:
        a static reference to @intrinsic("construct", UI appearance, @intrinsic("cast", a static reference to (the body's rules), a pointer to UI appearance rule), the length of (the body's rules))

section when viewport is below {a value:width}:
    result: UI appearance rule
    body:
        rules: many UI appearance rule
    value:
        @intrinsic("construct", UI appearance rule, 100, width as a floating-point number, UI ink 0 0 0, "", a static reference to @intrinsic("construct", UI appearance, @intrinsic("cast", a static reference to (the body's rules), a pointer to UI appearance rule), the length of (the body's rules)))

use {UI appearance reference:appearance} means: @intrinsic("construct", UI appearance rule, 0, 0.0, UI ink 0 0 0, "", appearance)
padding is {a value:number} means: UI appearance rule 1 valued number
gap is {a value:number} means: UI appearance rule 2 valued number
maximum width is {a value:number} means: UI appearance rule 3 valued number
font size is {integer:number} means: UI appearance rule 4 valued number
line spacing is {a value:number} means: UI appearance rule 5 valued number
text is {UI paint:ink} means: UI appearance rule 6 colored ink
background is {UI paint:ink} means: UI appearance rule 7 colored ink
corner radius is {a value:number} means: UI appearance rule 8 valued number
border width is {a value:number} means: UI appearance rule 9 valued number
border is {UI paint:ink} means: UI appearance rule 10 colored ink
columns are {integer:number} means: UI appearance rule 11 valued number
stack below {a value:number} means: UI appearance rule 12 valued number
minimum height is {a value:number} means: UI appearance rule 13 valued number
text is centered means: UI appearance rule 14 valued 1
flow is horizontal means: UI appearance rule 15 valued 1
font is {C string:path} means: @intrinsic("construct", UI appearance rule, 16, 0.0, UI ink 0 0 0, path, no UI appearance)
position is sticky means: UI appearance rule 17 valued 1
minimum width is {a value:number} means: UI appearance rule 18 valued number
content is hidden means: UI appearance rule 19 valued 1
height is {a value:number} means: UI appearance rule 20 valued number
font is bold means: UI appearance rule 21 valued 1
lines do not wrap means: UI appearance rule 22 valued 1
flow is overlay means: UI appearance rule 23 valued 1
image fit is contain means: UI appearance rule 24 valued 0
image fit is cover means: UI appearance rule 24 valued 1
image fit is stretch means: UI appearance rule 24 valued 2
aspect ratio is {a value:width} by {a value:height} means: UI appearance rule 25 valued ((width as a floating-point number) / (height as a floating-point number))

class:
    patterns:
        UI appearance settings
    members:
        padding as a floating-point number
        gap as a floating-point number
        maximum width as a floating-point number
        font size as an integer
        line spacing as a floating-point number
        foreground as UI paint
        background as UI paint
        filled as a boolean
        radius as a floating-point number
        border width as a floating-point number
        border ink as UI paint
        columns as an integer
        stack below as a floating-point number
        minimum height as a floating-point number
        centered as a boolean
        horizontal as a boolean
        font path as a C string
        sticky as a boolean
        minimum width as a floating-point number
        hidden as a boolean
        height as a floating-point number
        bold as a boolean
        unwrapped as a boolean
        overlay as a boolean
        image fit as an integer
        aspect ratio as a floating-point number

to get default UI appearance settings:
    set result to a new UI appearance settings
    set result's font size to 16
    set result's line spacing to 1.5
    set result's foreground to UI ink 25 29 35
    set result's columns to 1
    set result's font path to ""
    return result

to apply UI appearance {UI appearance reference:appearance} for {floating-point number:viewport} to {a pointer to UI appearance settings:settings}:
    set index to 0
    loop while index < appearance's count:
        set rule to the item at index in (appearance's rules)
        set kind to rule's kind
        if (kind = 0) or ((kind = 100) and (viewport < rule's number)):
            apply UI appearance (rule's appearance) for viewport to settings
        if kind = 1:
            set settings's padding to rule's number
        if kind = 2:
            set settings's gap to rule's number
        if kind = 3:
            set settings's maximum width to rule's number
        if kind = 4:
            set settings's font size to rule's number as an integer
        if kind = 5:
            set settings's line spacing to rule's number
        if kind = 6:
            set settings's foreground to rule's ink
        if kind = 7:
            set settings's background to rule's ink
            set settings's filled to true
        if kind = 8:
            set settings's radius to rule's number
        if kind = 9:
            set settings's border width to rule's number
        if kind = 10:
            set settings's border ink to rule's ink
        if kind = 11:
            set settings's columns to rule's number as an integer
        if kind = 12:
            set settings's stack below to rule's number
        if kind = 13:
            set settings's minimum height to rule's number
        if kind = 14:
            set settings's centered to rule's number != 0.0
        if kind = 15:
            set settings's horizontal to rule's number != 0.0
        if kind = 16:
            set settings's font path to rule's text
        if kind = 17:
            set settings's sticky to rule's number != 0.0
        if kind = 18:
            set settings's minimum width to rule's number
        if kind = 19:
            set settings's hidden to rule's number != 0.0
        if kind = 20:
            set settings's height to rule's number
        if kind = 21:
            set settings's bold to rule's number != 0.0
        if kind = 22:
            set settings's unwrapped to rule's number != 0.0
        if kind = 23:
            set settings's overlay to rule's number != 0.0
        if kind = 24:
            set settings's image fit to rule's number as an integer
        if kind = 25:
            require condition ((rule's number > 0.0) and (rule's number is finite)) reporting "A UI aspect ratio must be positive and finite"
            set settings's aspect ratio to rule's number
        increment index

to get UI appearance {UI appearance reference:appearance} resolved for {floating-point number:viewport}:
    set result to default UI appearance settings
    apply UI appearance appearance for viewport to (the address of result)
    require condition ((result's font size > 0) and (result's line spacing > 0.0)) reporting "Text size and line spacing must be positive"
    require condition ((result's padding >= 0.0) and (result's columns > 0)) reporting "Appearance padding and columns must be valid"
    return result
